<title>UK: UK unemployment falls 95,800 in November.</title>
<headline>UK unemployment falls 95,800 in November.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics released the following provisional data for unemployment in November and average earnings in October. (Previous estimates in brackets, minus denotes fall, data seasonally adjusted unless indicated)</p>
<p>   UNEMPLOYMENT			NOV	 OCT   (OCT PREL)</p>
<p>    Monthly change		  -95,800*  -45,600  (-40,800)</p>
<p>    Rate (pct)			 6.9	 7.2	   (7.2)</p>
<p>    Monthly non-s/adj change    -105,800   n/a     (-126,500)</p>
<p>    Monthly non-s/adj rate (pct) 6.7	 7.1	   (7.1)</p>
<p>NOTE - Mkts forecast 25,000 November unemployment fall  </p>
<p>    Unemployment level (million)     1.929     2.025     (2.030)</p>
<p>    Unemployment level unadj     1.871     1.977     (1.977)</p>
<p>    Avg change in past 3m adj   -59,800   -33,600  (-32,000)</p>
<p>    Avg change in past 6m	 -39,500   -26,200  (-25,400)</p>
<p>    AVERAGE EARNINGS		  OCT	 SEPT   (SEPT PREL)</p>
<p>    underlying yearly chng (pct)  4.0	 4.0	  (4.0)</p>
<p>    index (base 1990)		133.7     133.4     (133.3)</p>
<p>    actual yearly chng (pct)	3.8	 4.2	  (4.1)</p>
<p>By sector (annual pct chng)</p>
<p>    Production-- underlying	 4.25	4.25	(4.25)</p>
<p>		  -- actual	     3.8	 4.3	  (4.3)</p>
<p>    manufacturing-- underlying    4.25	4.5	  (4.5)</p>
<p>		     -- actual	  4.0	 4.7	  (4.6)</p>
<p>    Services     -- underlying    4.0	 3.75	(3.75)</p>
<p>		     -- actual	  3.8	 4.0	  (4.0)</p>
<p>NOTE-consensus forecast 4.0 pct for underlying average earnings</p>
<p>    UNIT WAGE COSTS	    OCT	  SEPT    (PREL SEPT)</p>
<p>    Monthly change vs yr ago 3.5	  4.8	 (5.4)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)	  114.0	114.2   (114.9)</p>
<p>    3-mth versus same yr/ago 4.6	  4.7	 (5.2)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)	  114.2	114.2   (114.7)</p>
<p>    Job centre vacancies    NOV	   OCT     (PREV OCT)</p>
<p>    Change			+7,100	+9,000   (9,300)</p>
<p>    Level			 269,700     262,600  (262,900)</p>
<p>    Avge 3-m change	   +10,900     +10,800   (10,900)</p>
<p>* November's fall in unemployment is the largest since January 1971, when the series began, the ONS said.</p>
<p>The ONS said about 20,000 of the total 95,800 fall in jobless in November was due to the backlog of claims built up by the introduction of the jobseekers allowance scheme in October.</p>
<p>A further 5,000 is due to bringing forward means testing to six months.</p>
